# Manually correct the authoritative board state — a backup for when
# automatic vision-based move detection misreads the physical board. Applied
# under the game loop thread's control (same event-handoff pattern as
# /game/resign and /game/new_game), not directly from the service callback.
# FEN-replacement only (not structured move/capture/castling actions) — this
# is what a drag-and-drop board editor naturally produces. Castling rights
# and en-passant target are whatever the submitted FEN says (a full FEN
# string, not just the piece-placement field) — the caller is responsible
# for those if they matter; a plain drag-edit UI will typically submit them
# cleared/default.
string fen
---
bool success
string message
